                        <forename>John Thomas</forename>
                        <surname>Smith</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1766-06-23">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1833-03-06"/>
                    <occupation>printmaker</occupation>
                    <occupation>draughtsman</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Smith studied engraving with John Keyse Sherwin and subsequently developed an interested in antiquarianism. He published his drawings in 
      <title>Antiquities of London</title> (1791–1800) and <title>Ancient Topography of London</title> (1810–15). He became keeper of prints and drawings 
      at the British Museum in 1816.</p>
                        <p>Identification not certain; however, one of the meetings was an adv at artist <persName key="NOR01">James Northcote's</persName>. 
      He was also associated with the Society for Antiquaries; Godwin knew many of this group's members..</p>
                    </note>
